# Card packing & responsive rules

A horizontal row of cards must fill 100% of the content width. Do not leave an empty track to the right of the last card (Favorites Wales is the example). If a row would end short, place one or two sibling cards that fit the leftover width, or let the last-row items grow so the row stays full.

Cards in the same row share one height. A short text fact next to a taller neighbor stretches to that height. Title stays top-left. Number and description pin to the bottom-left.

Do not stretch one text-only fact beside a tall story card or chart card. Put two, three, or four facts in a vertical stack (`col-stack`) on the side instead:
- Home Barcelona: 4 facts stacked vertically on the right of Barcelona story card on desktop.
- Home Real Madrid 15 Cups: 3 facts stacked vertically on the right on desktop.
- Player Stats (Mbappe): 2 facts stacked vertically on the left of Real Madrid 15 Cups card.
- Tournaments (Euro 2008): 2 facts stacked vertically on the right of Euro 2008 banner (Euro 2008 card height reduced to match 2 facts).

Proportional Scaling of Charts & Graphics:
- When a card with graphics (`MixChart`, `DotGrid`) stretches vertically to match a taller neighbor or stack, the graphic scales proportionally to fill the available space inside the card.
- `MixChart` bars (Barcelona, Wales) scale height proportionally with available slot height.
- `DotGrid` dots / grid (Real Madrid cups) scale up proportionally to fill leftover vertical height in the card.

Circle Cards & Horizontal Layout:
- Story cards with circles (Zidane): hug content height. Circles sit on one horizontal row at the bottom (`flex-wrap: nowrap`). Do not stretch empty space under the circles.
- Favorites screen: cards have wider min-width (~340–360px) so circle stats sit side-by-side horizontally in one row without vertical wrapping, fitting 3–4 cards per row on desktop instead of squishing 6 cards.
- Tournaments screen match row (`2:0 Wales`, `1:0 Croatia`): includes a 3rd match card (`1-0 France`) on desktop to avoid overly wide cards.

Inner inset on every card is `--size-card-pad` (`space/l`, 20px). Do not mix `l` and `xl` on card edges.

On viewports ≤900px (tablet/mobile), main story cards stay in reading order. Fact stacks move cleanly to the bottom of the page so the screen is not a long vertical list of interspersed facts.

Do not fade or slide the chrome when switching routes. Tab changes must not flicker.
